.TH HU_SSH 3 "" "helios-unix" "Library functions"
.SH NAME
hu_ssh_open, hu_ssh_open_fd, hu_ssh_status, hu_ssh_trust, hu_ssh_authenticate, hu_ssh_resize, hu_ssh_read, hu_ssh_write, hu_ssh_send_eof, hu_ssh_interest, hu_ssh_wait_fd, hu_ssh_close \- use an SSH session
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <helios/unix/ssh.h>

struct hu_ssh *hu_ssh_open(const struct hu_ssh_backend *backend,
    const struct hu_ssh_options *options,
    const struct hu_ssh_transport *transport);
struct hu_ssh *hu_ssh_open_fd(const struct hu_ssh_options *, int fd);
int hu_ssh_status(struct hu_ssh *, struct hu_ssh_info *);
int hu_ssh_trust(struct hu_ssh *, int accept);
int hu_ssh_authenticate(struct hu_ssh *, const struct hu_ssh_auth *);
int hu_ssh_resize(struct hu_ssh *, unsigned columns, unsigned rows);
int hu_ssh_read(struct hu_ssh *, void *, unsigned);
int hu_ssh_write(struct hu_ssh *, const void *, unsigned);
int hu_ssh_send_eof(struct hu_ssh *);
int hu_ssh_interest(struct hu_ssh *, int operation, struct hu_ssh_wait *);
int hu_ssh_wait_fd(struct hu_ssh *);
void hu_ssh_close(struct hu_ssh *);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This interface describes an SSH session independently of where the SSH engine
runs. A provider can implement the protocol over byte callbacks or offload it
to a host. No native Transputer crypto provider is included.
.PP
options supplies host, user, port, terminal, optional command, initial columns
and rows, pty, timeout_ms and optional provider configuration. The default
provider accepts hosts up to 255 bytes, users and terminal names up to 63,
commands up to 767, and timeouts of 100..120000 milliseconds.
Keep options and its strings valid until close for providers that borrow them.
.SS Ownership
Open returns an object or NULL with errno set. A successful open takes
ownership of the transport; a failed open leaves it with the caller.
The callback table and context must outlive the object. ssh_backend.h defines
the provider and transport interfaces. A native engine needs read, write and
a select-compatible wait descriptor, and does not require transport controls.
.PP
open_fd is a convenience adapter for an already connected TCP descriptor.
It makes the descriptor nonblocking and takes ownership on success only.
Use the object for I/O afterward; do not close its descriptor separately.
.SS Connection and authentication
Call status to drive and inspect negotiation. States are CONNECTING, HOSTKEY,
AUTH, OPENING, READY, CLOSED and FAILED, with the HU_SSH_ prefix.
At HOSTKEY, inspect key_type and fingerprint, then explicitly call trust.
At AUTH, inspect auth_methods and supply HU_SSH_PASSWORD or HU_SSH_PUBLICKEY
with authenticate. secret is the password or private-key passphrase; key and
key_size contain private-key data for public-key authentication (at most
HU_SSH_MAX_KEY bytes). auth_attempt increments after unsuccessful attempts.
The supplied provider copies credentials before authenticate returns.
.PP
status also supplies a diagnostic message and provider error. At CLOSED,
exit_valid indicates whether exit_status is available. Drain pending output
even if status already reports CLOSED.
.SS I/O and event loops
Read and write return byte counts, or -1 with errno set. Read returns zero at
EOF. Handle short writes and retry EAGAIN/EWOULDBLOCK/EINTR without losing
unaccepted data. EAGAIN and EWOULDBLOCK have different values on Helios.
The supplied terminal provider merges remote stdout and stderr.
.PP
interest supplies the transport descriptor, readiness events and timeout_ms
for HU_SSH_READ, HU_SSH_WRITE or HU_SSH_PROGRESS. Events are HU_SSH_WAIT_READ
and HU_SSH_WAIT_WRITE. A read can need writability and a write can need
readability in a native engine. A negative timeout means no timer; zero means
retry immediately. Wait for the requested readiness or timer, then retry the
operation (status for progress). An object belongs to one application thread.
.PP
resize sends new columns and rows for an established remote terminal.
Call it from the event loop after SIGWINCH, not inside the signal handler.
send_eof half-closes input after accepted writes have drained; output remains
readable. close cancels the session and frees its engine and owned transport
exactly once. NULL is accepted. It does not wait for the remote program.
.SH PROVIDERS
The default uses the Linux I/O server's optional HSH1 SSH service. Control
framing is private to its transport adapter. Native providers use the same
application interface and may use configuration for engine-specific services.
HU_SSH_DEFAULT_BACKEND can select another provider when building the library.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Open returns an object or NULL. I/O returns bytes, EOF or -1. Other calls
return 0 or -1 with errno set, except wait_fd, which returns the descriptor.
.SH SEE ALSO
ssh(1), hu_tls(3), hu_terminal(3), helios-unix(7)
